[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5800246583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123733#issuecomment-5800246583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123733","id":5800246583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWbi9Nw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:06:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:08:47Z","body":"> Slightly unrelated, but I'm not sure why in the mobile renderer reflections seem to be way overly bright, could this be a color space issue?\r\n\r\nCheck if it still occurs with **HDR 2D** enabled in the Project Settings (then restart the editor). Enabling HDR 2D in Mobile switches to 16 bpc rendering like Forward+, which removes the need for the 2.0 brightness multiplier trick.\r\n\r\nIf the bug disappears in this case, then it's an issue of the brightness multiplier not being accounted for somewhere. Regardless, this should be fixed in a separate PR as the issue is also present in `master`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/go